00:15:39.720 --> 00:15:42.780
Well, you know, all that polite business and smiling at everybody

00:15:42.780 --> 00:15:45.930
and saying hello and calling Dad Sir Mr. Cleaver.

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:49.450
Well, you know, Beaver, there's nothing wrong with being polite.

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:52.470
Yeah, somehow when Eddie's polite,

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:55.500
I always think the guy he's being polite to is getting the worst of it.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:59.140
Well, you know, Beaver, I'm not sure.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.940
but I think this polite business with Eddie

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:03.140
is sort of a camouflage.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:05.380
Camouflage?

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:06.660
Mm-hmm.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:09.580
Gee, Mom, do you mean like when they paint stripes on airplanes?

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:13.140
I mean sort of a cover-up for another Eddie.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:15.130
Gosh, Mom, you mean there's another Eddie?

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:17.130
Well, Beaver, in a sense there is,

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.450
and I'm afraid we don't know him.

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:21.610
